from sys-underground-kit.replay
# sys-fossil-revival (scripts_mining_museum.s, scrcmd_fossil.c): with the Explorer Kit the
# Oreburgh Mining Museum's researcher revives fossils. Two fossils: get_fossil_count is 2, the menu lists both (the
# ROM's fossil table order), the Skull Fossil is picked (get_species_from_fossil: Cranidos) and taken; out of the
# museum and back, Cranidos comes at level 20 (no nickname).
# Setup: a Skull Fossil and an Armor Fossil (what an even and an odd trainer id dig: sMiningObjects' weights).
give item platinum:ITEM_SKULL_FOSSIL 1
give item platinum:ITEM_ARMOR_FOSSIL 1
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_MINING_MUSEUM 6 5 up
until idle
+0 press a
+1 release a
advance text
+0 press a
+1 release a
until menu
+10 press down
+1 release down
+2 press a
+1 release a
advance text
until idle
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_REVIVED_POKEMON_SPECIES 408
+0 assert state bag.items [{"item":"platinum:ITEM_ARMOR_FOSSIL","count":1}]
# Out and back in (the map-local flag clears), then the researcher again.
+0 press left
until position 5 5
+0 release left
until idle
+0 press down
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_OREBURGH_CITY"
+0 release down
until idle
+0 press down
until position 305 748
+0 release down
until idle
+0 press up
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_MINING_MUSEUM"
+0 release up
until idle
+0 press up
until position 5 5
+0 release up
until idle
+0 press right
until position 6 5
+0 release right
until idle
+0 press up
+1 release up
+4 press a
+5 release a
advance text
+0 press b
+1 release b
until idle
+0 assert party 1 platinum:SPECIES_CRANIDOS
+0 assert state party[1].level 20
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_REVIVED_POKEMON_SPECIES 0
